// E0111: a deeply right-nested assignment chain (`a = b = c = ...`)
// recurses once per `=` through parse_assignment with no bracketing token
// to bound it.  It must hit the parser's recursion limit and emit a clean
// diagnostic instead of overflowing the native stack (SIGSEGV).  400 levels
// is well past the 256 limit.
